Examples to the nonequispaced fast cosine transform

Author

  Stefan Kunis <kunis@mathematik.tu-chemnitz.de>
  Steffen Klatt <heracleum.mantegazziani@web.de>

List of files and purpose

  README            this file
  simple_test.c     introductory example how to use the nfct

Compiling

  simple_test.c includes nfft3mp.h, which selects the floating-point precision
  from a preprocessor macro. The build system defines it. To compile such a
  program yourself, define the macro that matches the installed library, e.g.
  for double precision

    gcc -DNFFT_PRECISION_DOUBLE simple_test.c -lnfft3 -lfftw3 -lm

  or use NFFT_PRECISION_SINGLE with -lnfft3f -lfftw3f, or
  NFFT_PRECISION_LONG_DOUBLE with -lnfft3l -lfftw3l.

References

  M. Fenn and D. Potts.
  Fast summation based on fast trigonometric transforms at nonequispaced nodes.
  Numer. Linear Algebra Appl., 12:161--169, 2005.
